We're back from the coast, and I promised you a full report.

I finally got round to framing the map you gave us. It is hanging in the hall=
 now, and visitors always stop to look for the places they know.

The repairs to the roof are done at last. The builders were tidy and quick on=
ce they started, and we no longer need the bucket in the attic when it rains.

We finally finished painting the spare room. It took far longer than planned,=
 mostly because we changed our minds about the colour twice, but it looks muc=
h brighter now.

The kittens next door have discovered our garden. They chase leaves across th=
e lawn every afternoon, and I confess I spend far too long watching them from=
 the window.

We went to the farmers' market on Saturday and came home with far too much ch=
eese. The bread stall was excellent too, and the man there remembered us from=
 last time.

It was good to hear your news on the phone. I am glad the new job is going we=
ll, and that the journey is shorter than you expected once you found the righ=
t train.

I took up watercolours again after many years. My first few attempts were mud=
dy, but the evening class has helped, and I am quite pleased with a painting =
of the harbour.

The school play was a great success. The children had clearly practised for w=
eeks, and the costumes were remarkable considering most of them were made fro=
m old curtains.

The local library has started a repair cafe once a month. I took the old lamp=
 along, and a retired electrician had it working again within twenty minutes.

The photos from the wedding came out beautifully. I will put a few in the pos=
t for you, as I know you prefer prints to looking at them on a screen.

The hedge finally got its trim on Saturday. It took most of the morning, and =
the garden waste bin is full, but the front of the house looks much tidier fo=
r it.

We watched the meteor shower from the back garden last night. It was cold, bu=
t we saw several bright ones, and the children talked about it all through br=
eakfast.

I'll bring the photos when we see you next.

